<http://data.silknow.org/object/8791d119-9fa6-3ac4-8b87-84d90223ede1>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered, 1600-1629, English"@en , "Chalice veil of fine linen embroidered with red silk in double running, stem, braid and buttonhole stitch.\n\nIn its centre is a rayed medallion containing the sacred monogram 'IHS', the cross and the sacred heart. In each corner is a winged angel's head. There is a border of 30 square compartments outlined by narrow bands of geometrical ornament, each filled with an emblem of an instrument of the Passion, there being 9 different motifs in total. The emblems represented are as follows: the Crown of Thorns and the Veil of St. Veronica (<i>Sudarium</i>); sword, halberd, lance, purse and lantern; pillar, handkerchief(?) and the cock; pincers, hammer and 3 nails; cross with sun and moon above; ladder, spear and sponge on reed; 4 scourges; a coat and 3 dice; a tomb, or the Ark of the Covenant.\n\nThere are several holes and areas of wear in the centre of the field."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/332bdf12-f044-3b8a-a78b-6552c7e95761> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/a7dd27b4-6348-344f-b3ed-fe2d63d5f602> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d824deab-c51b-37e3-8887-603844b56fd7> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Chalice veil of fine linen embroidered with red silk in double running, stem, braid and buttonhole stitch.\n\nIn its centre is a rayed medallion containing the sacred monogram 'IHS', the cross and the sacred heart. In each corner is a winged angel's head. There is a border of 30 square compartments outlined by narrow bands of geometrical ornament, each filled with an emblem of an instrument of the Passion, there being 9 different motifs in total. The emblems represented are as follows: the Crown of Thorns and the Veil of St. Veronica (<i>Sudarium</i>); sword, halberd, lance, purse and lantern; pillar, handkerchief(?) and the cock; pincers, hammer and 3 nails; cross with sun and moon above; ladder, spear and sponge on reed; 4 scourges; a coat and 3 dice; a tomb, or the Ark of the Covenant.\n\nThere are several holes and areas of wear in the centre of the field."@en , "embroidered, 1600-1629, English"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/8791d119-9fa6-3ac4-8b87-84d90223ede1/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/8791d119-9fa6-3ac4-8b87-84d90223ede1/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.1-1914" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O364620> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/8791d119-9fa6-3ac4-8b87-84d90223ede1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Chalice veil of fine linen embroidered with red silk in double running, stem, braid and buttonhole stitch.\n\nIn its centre is a rayed medallion containing the sacred monogram 'IHS', the cross and the sacred heart. In each corner is a winged angel's head. There is a border of 30 square compartments outlined by narrow bands of geometrical ornament, each filled with an emblem of an instrument of the Passion, there being 9 different motifs in total. The emblems represented are as follows: the Crown of Thorns and the Veil of St. Veronica (<i>Sudarium</i>); sword, halberd, lance, purse and lantern; pillar, handkerchief(?) and the cock; pincers, hammer and 3 nails; cross with sun and moon above; ladder, spear and sponge on reed; 4 scourges; a coat and 3 dice; a tomb, or the Ark of the Covenant.\n\nThere are several holes and areas of wear in the centre of the field."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8791d119-9fa6-3ac4-8b87-84d90223ede1> .

